        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-208",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "jose.jwe decryption verifies the CBC-HMAC authentication tag (used for A128CBC-HS256/A192CBC-HS384/A256CBC-HS512 per RFC 7518 \u00a75.2) with a plain, non-constant-time Python `!=` comparison instead of a constant-time comparison such as hmac.compare_digest. The expected tag is computed via HMAC in `_auth_tag` and compared to the attacker-supplied tag from the token with `auth_tag != auth_tag_check` \u2014 this short-circuits byte-by-byte, creating an observable timing side channel that could in principle assist a MAC-forgery/timing attack against CBC-HMAC JWE tokens. The library already correctly uses `hmac.compare_digest` elsewhere (JWS HMAC verification in native.py line 69), showing the safe pattern exists in this codebase but is absent here.\n\nVerifier (CONFIRM): Verified directly against source and the code graph. jose/jwe.py's `_decrypt_and_auth` computes the expected CBC-HMAC tag (`_auth_tag`, lines 557-574, using `mac_key.sign()` i.e. raw HMAC digest) and compares it to the attacker-supplied tag with the plain Python operator `auth_tag != auth_tag_check` (line 240), raising on mismatch (line 241). Python bytes `!=`/`==` is not guaranteed constant-time (CPython short-circuits/length-checks), unlike `hmac.compare_digest`. Crucially, I confirmed via jose/backends/cryptography_backend.py:490-513 that for the CBC branch (`mode.name != \"GCM\"`), `CryptographyAESKey.decrypt()` performs plain AES-CBC decrypt + PKCS7 unpad and completely ignores the `tag` argument \u2014 so the `!=` check in jwe.py:240 is the ONLY place the CBC-HMAC auth tag is ever verified for A128CBC-HS256/A192CBC-HS384/A256CBC-HS512. This is the same timing-oracle class exploited historically against CBC-then-MAC constructs (e.g. the \"Lucky 13\" attack). By contrast, jose/backends/native.py:68-69 shows the codebase does know and use the safe `hmac.compare_digest(sig, self.sign(msg))` pattern for JWS HMAC verification \u2014 confirming the safe pattern exists but was not applied in jwe.py. Graph query also confirms `ALGORITHMS.HMAC_AUTH_TAG = {A128CBC_HS256, A192CBC_HS384, A256CBC_HS512}` (constants.py:67) matches RFC7518 \u00a75.2 CBC-HMAC algs, and that the `auth_tag != auth_tag_check` CpgCall (uid 7148c45e...) at jwe.py:240 has `reachable_from_entry=true, hop_distance=1`, i.e. statically reachable from an entry point in this scan. exploit_search catalog was unavailable in this environment (\"not indexed\"), so no Metasploit-module cross-check could be performed; this does not affect the source-level finding."
          },
